# Spring Boot / Java 25 — apptdea

Apply these conventions on every change to this project.

## Stack

- Spring Boot 4.x, Maven, package base `com.udea.apptdea`
- Data: Spring Data JPA + PostgreSQL
- API docs: springdoc-openapi
- Prefer modern Java (records, pattern matching, sealed types, virtual threads where appropriate)

## Naming (always English)

- Classes, interfaces, methods, fields, parameters, packages, and constants: **English only**
- Controllers: `*Controller` · Services: `*Service` · Repositories: `*Repository`
- Entities: domain nouns (`User`, `Order`) · Exceptions: `*Exception`
- Packages: lowercase (`controller`, `service`, `repository`, `domain`, `dto`, `config`, `mapper`)

## Javadoc (mandatory)

- Every **public** method must have up-to-date Javadoc (`@param`, `@return`, `@throws` when relevant)
- Public classes and records: class-level Javadoc describing responsibility
- Update Javadoc when behavior or signature changes — never leave stale docs

```java
/**
 * Creates a new user from the given request.
 *
 * @param request payload with user data
 * @return the persisted user as a response DTO
 * @throws UserAlreadyExistsException if email is already registered
 */
public UserResponse create(CreateUserRequest request) { ... }
```

## DTOs

- Use **Java records** for all request/response DTOs — no mutable DTO classes
- Place under `com.udea.apptdea.dto` (or feature subpackages)
- Prefer validation annotations on record components (`@NotBlank`, `@Email`, etc.)

```java
public record CreateUserRequest(
    @NotBlank String email,
    @NotBlank String fullName
) {}
```

## Layering

| Layer | Package | Responsibility |
|-------|---------|----------------|
| Controller | `...controller` | HTTP only; validate input; map to/from DTOs |
| Service | `...service` | Business logic; transactions (`@Transactional`) |
| Repository | `...repository` | Persistence; Spring Data interfaces |
| Domain | `...domain` / `...entity` | JPA entities |
| DTO | `...dto` | Records for API contracts |
| Config | `...config` | `@Configuration` beans |

- Constructor injection only (no `@Autowired` on fields)
- Prefer `@RestController` + `@RequestMapping` / HTTP verb mappings
- Return DTOs from controllers — never expose JPA entities in the API
- Keep services focused; avoid fat controllers

## Java / Spring practices

- Prefer `Optional` at service boundaries; do not return `null` from public APIs
- Use pattern matching (`instanceof`, `switch`) instead of cascading casts
- Prefer sealed hierarchies for closed domain/error types when useful
- Prefer virtual threads for blocking I/O-bound workloads when enabled in the app
- Fail fast with clear domain exceptions; map them via `@ControllerAdvice`
- Keep methods small and single-purpose; avoid deep nesting
- Prefer immutable data and final fields where possible
- Configuration via `application.properties` / profiles — no hardcoded secrets

## Testing

- Mirror package structure under `src/test/java`
- Unit-test services; slice/integration-test controllers and repositories as needed
- Public test helpers follow the same naming and Javadoc rules when public

## Project structure

```
apptdea/
├── pom.xml
├── mvnw / mvnw.cmd
├── .cursor/rules/
│   └── springboot.mdc
├── src/
│   ├── main/
│   │   ├── java/com/udea/apptdea/
│   │   │   └── ApptdeaApplication.java
│   │   └── resources/
│   │       ├── application.properties
│   │       ├── static/
│   │       └── templates/
│   └── test/
│       └── java/com/udea/apptdea/
│           └── ApptdeaApplicationTests.java
```

When adding features, extend under `com.udea.apptdea` with the layer packages above (do not invent alternate roots).
